# The unit tests: the checks of the repo's .clang-tidy, without those that
# only meet test idioms.
#   bugprone-unchecked-optional-access  REQUIRE(x) before *x is a check the
#       analysis does not see (Catch2's macro)
#   bugprone-unused-return-value  the tests' helpers call a document method
#       for its effect and check the document afterwards
#   bugprone-random-generator-seed  a fixed seed is what makes a test
#       repeat
#   bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-conversion  sscanf and atoi read
#       the tests' own recordings and switches, whose form the tests fix
#   concurrency-mt-unsafe  getenv for a test's switch, before its threads
#   performance-*  a test is not a hot path: its callbacks take an
#       Assembly by value as AssemblyCallback hands it over, and its
#       lists are filled without a reserve
---
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  -bugprone-unused-return-value,
  -bugprone-random-generator-seed,
  -bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-conversion,
  -concurrency-mt-unsafe,
  -performance-*
...
